WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.409
A lot of people have asked me what it was
like to wake up to the images that were coming

00:00:03.409 --> 00:00:07.609
out of Syria with the victims of the sarin
gas attack.

00:00:07.609 --> 00:00:13.000
“Witnesses and some activists said the toxic
substance was delivered by Syrian and Russian

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.920
jets in an attack in the rebel-held region.”

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:20.869
Obviously it was painful, it was infuriating,
it was frustrating, but at the same time,

00:00:20.869 --> 00:00:28.550
there have been so many mornings like that
in the last six years.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:39.730
It is an interesting, sort of, you know, question
as to why we object to the methods of slaughter

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:45.300
but not the overall slaughter that the Syrian
people have been facing over the last six

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.080
years.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:56.170
Syrians have been dying by bullet, by mortar,
by barrel bomb.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:01:01.130
And they've been killed both by the regime
and the armed opposition to the regime.

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:07.070
I think a lot of people paid attention recently
because there's something horrific about death

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:09.369
by air, death by breathing in chemicals.

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:14.140
There's something that's sort of tantalizing
about the horrificness of evil.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:18.900
It's a way that you can see it in a more blatant
way.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.509
I think we've become a little desensitized
to the other kinds of death.

00:01:22.509 --> 00:01:28.929
The problem is after so many years of dehumanizing
Arabs and Muslims and Syrians in the global

00:01:28.929 --> 00:01:29.929
imagination...

00:01:29.929 --> 00:01:32.119
Do you think Islam is at war with the West?

00:01:32.119 --> 00:01:34.830
I think Islam hates us.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:40.369
..that kind of dehumanization has led people
to sort of tune out and to think that what's

00:01:40.369 --> 00:01:42.891
happening there is sort of inevitable.

00:01:42.891 --> 00:01:45.319
This is a question of culture, a question
of religion.

00:01:45.319 --> 00:01:49.069
I think part of the reason we're willing to
let Syria go or let these sorts of things

00:01:49.069 --> 00:01:53.299
happen is because we've become accustomed
to really simplistic narratives about Arabs

00:01:53.299 --> 00:01:54.299
and Muslims.

00:01:54.299 --> 00:01:58.090
They will never have refugees or “rapeugees”
in their backyards.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:01:59.109
They just will not.

00:01:59.109 --> 00:02:02.929
This is part of the problem, is that we have
no idea who Syrians are.

00:02:02.929 --> 00:02:06.939
We have no idea what Syria is, even though
it's this place of great culture and great

00:02:06.939 --> 00:02:08.690
civilization and great humanity.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:13.290
If it's consuming our headlines, yeah, it's
probably at that point risen to the level

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.230
where we should take the time to learn something.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:20.540
I think the American public in many ways has
its own problems, but it has to realize that

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.370
we are implicated in what's going on in Syria.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:28.720
In the last six years, it has been unfortunately
only mostly Syrians mourning the loss of Syria,

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.310
but this is something that the whole global
community should feel the loss of, because

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:33.879
it's our loss collectively.

00:02:33.879 --> 00:02:38.650
The places might not completely disappear,
but the people who make those places are going

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:40.090
to have disappeared.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:43.989
It would be a tragedy if we only found out
about it too late, once we couldn't do anything

00:02:43.989 --> 00:02:44.469
about it.

